A||N||7||fierobaby||frying the starter?||||1||
Z||000000||fierobaby||10-12-2001||04:04 PM||||ok so heres my problem... I have an 84 4 cyl automatic... the car will start and run ok for a bit... but once it starts to get hotter it begins to want to stall and sputter. It doesnot even start when it is warm at all. the car died awhile ago and we put started fluid in and it started. I was wondering if maybe the heat is getting to my starter? if it is how can I stop it?<P>------------------<BR>:wtf:<FONT COLOR="LETTER"> AIM: Fierobaby87:wtf:<BR>http://angelfire.com/sports/sfiero </FONT><BR>           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||JohnF||10-12-2001||04:17 PM||||You state it won't start when warm.  <P>You didn't say if the starter turned when engine was hot.  If starter turns, it isn't starter.  If starter doesn't turn, it is.  Just that simple to rule out (or in) starter.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierowrecker||10-12-2001||06:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierobaby:<BR><B>ok so heres my problem... I have an 84 4 cyl automatic... the car will start and run ok for a bit... but once it starts to get hotter it begins to want to stall and sputter. It doesnot even start when it is warm at all. the car died awhile ago and we put started fluid in and it started. I was wondering if maybe the heat is getting to my starter? if it is how can I stop it?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Babe!<BR>Sounds more like a fuel starvation problem...<BR>If it rolls over, but won't fire untill you squirt starter fluid, then you have spark, but no fuel...<BR>crash...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||maryjane||10-12-2001||06:24 PM||||hmm. sounds like maybe you're describing 2 separate problems, both heat related. Starter<BR>problems show up when hot more often than not (but not always). Electronics give more problems when warm also. Start with the battery, if the eng won't turn over when hot.<BR>Have it checked at an Auto Zone,etc. If it's ok, check your + & - battery cables. Still won't turn over? Time to pull & check the starter. They may be able to check it while it's still on the car, I haven't had it done in a long time. If it cranks over, but won't fire, it could be several things. Look down the throttle body & see if you can see any fuel being injected, & check for spark. No spark is usually caused by module in distributor, but could also be the coil. No fuel could be the pump, fuel pump relay, oil press switch, ecm or associated wiring. My 84SE auto has an occasional problem that is similar.When hot, it spins over, but won't start unless I pour a little gas down the TBI, or I let it cool off. Let us know what you find. getting any codes?<P>Don- 84SE 4cyl auto||||reg||1
Z||000004||JohnF||10-12-2001||07:06 PM||||As my Daddy used to say about Model "A"s.  Fire, fuel & air.  It takes all 3.  If you don't have one, which is it?  Go from there!||||reg||1
Z||000005||WhiteFieroBlur||10-13-2001||01:09 AM||||I had a problem with something like that, I would go driving in my car and when it gets hot it would just cut off on me where I was at. I could be driving down the street and it would shut off. It mainly did it at stop lights. and I would have to sit there and pass a few green lights before it would start and go again. So I did the usual and had the battery tested and everything was fine, so I was like whats going on. So I took it to the shop to see what the guy says.<BR>    <BR>  ok this is how he fixed it, he told me I had some stuff in my gas tank that was so crappy that gas would not eat thru it. So over time it got into my fuel system. I would hear this whistlng or some sound that sounds like my fuel filter, So he had to replace my gas tank and fuel pump an fuel filter and some otherfuel ralated parts. Now the reason it stopped is cause my fuel filter or pump got clogged and over heated so the car shuts down. so I sat there until it cooled down an would start up like nothing happened. Now my dumb self didn't have enough money to change the gas tank, so guess what? I think its doing it again cause I hear that strange noise again that sounds like my fuel flter is glogged. and it runs like crap at about 10 mph, bucks back and forth far too much. he told me its gonna be like 300 dllars again to change the tank.<P>  You know I swear my fiero is never gonna be happy. its like they are getting back at us for not making them anymore or something. No matter what I spend on the car it stays upset. and these are new parts I am giving it, I can not work on my car for nothing so everytime it breaks I pay the guy whatever to get new parts to fix it. the biggest was my clutch, he got about 700-800 dllars out of me to fix it.  <BR>  <BR>  well thats just my more than 2 cents about it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||SLYGUY||10-13-2001||02:44 PM||||Yea WhiteFieroBlur...<BR>I can do an awful lot of the minor repairs on my car, but some things I don't have the tools for. I can't find a way to stuff a full vehicle hoist into my tool box!!<BR>Seriously tho, I have a low whine coming from my clutch when I release the pedal. <BR>Used to be quiet when I engaged the clutch, but it is starting to make a little noise there too. <BR>I know...I know... It's the throw-out bearing. I'm going to have to have that replaced and while they are at it have a Borg-Warner clutch put in. I'll be forking over about the same amount to my local garage here soon. <BR>Did I mention they love to see me?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000007||WhiteFieroBlur||10-15-2001||01:27 AM||||I am hearing noise from my clutch also. When before I had a new one put in I did not hear any kind of noise from the clutch. Now since they all worked on my car and did whatever to it. I am hearing like air shoot out from my clutch as I release the clutch pedal. The same day I took it to a mechanic cause for some reason my back brakes were completely gone after having it towed. Hmm think maybe he didn't release the emergency brake? but the guy told me that it sounded like the clutch was in backwards. I was like wha? Well i took it to the guy and he laughed at me and told me that it was normal, Well it sure wasn't normal with the old clutch. Well people have told me that the clutch would not even work at all backwards so I figured its ok. its a kewl sound when moving from first gear and hearing my clutch engage. but it sure freaked me out at first.||||reg||1
